{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "librenms",
  "description": "A full LibreNMS collection: the unpaginated /devices table, per-device addresses and ports, and the estate-wide ARP and FDB tables. Envelope key order is status, devices, count, taken from api_success() in includes/html/api_functions.inc.php rather than from the doc, which prints them in a different order. Device rows carry the SELECT d.* field set including the SNMP credential columns, which is what a real server returns and which this integration must NOT write into runZero. ARP and FDB rows follow the vendor's own documented examples, with bare 12-hex MACs. Proves: /devices/{id}/ports is asked for ifPhysAddress explicitly, because the default response is ONLY ifName; the /devices/{id}/ip response merges v4 and v6 rows into one heterogeneous array; a device whose hostname is a bare IP contributes an address rather than a hostname; loopback and link-local are dropped; the ARP and FDB views of one MAC collapse into a single endpoint asset; and community, authpass, and cryptopass never reach a custom attribute. no_mac_in_id is skipped for the endpoint assets: an ARP or FDB row has no identifier but its MAC, and the id is paired with no-id-match no-id-break so it never drives a merge.",
